{
  "id": 21,
  "name": "sustained_regret_centrality",
  "intent": "Sustain regret weighting (0.30→0.22) instead of decaying to 0.10 so rank-based tie-breaking remains active throughout construction — uniform instances collapse absolute distance signals, so persistent regret is needed to disambiguate equally-near candidates. Add a decaying centrality bias via -mean_remaining so candidates nearer the geometric center of remaining cities win in noisy uniform layouts, producing a less-self-intersecting initial tour that 2-opt can refine cheaply. Cluster_density-modulated nearest_remaining and the progress-ramped return term are preserved to keep clustered and grid assembly intact. Hypothesis: sustained regret + early centrality yields a cleaner uniform start while clustered/grid remain dominated by their informative local distances and the return ramp.",
  "tags": [
    "regret",
    "progress"
  ],
  "code": "def priority(f):\n    progress = f[\"progress\"]\n    cluster_density = f[\"cluster_density\"]\n    distance = f[\"distance\"]\n    return_distance = f[\"return_distance\"]\n    nearest_remaining = f[\"nearest_remaining\"]\n    mean_remaining = f[\"mean_remaining\"]\n    regret = f[\"regret\"]\n    rw = 0.20 + 0.40 * progress\n    rgw = 0.30 - 0.08 * progress\n    cl_term = 0.10 * cluster_density * (1.0 - progress) * nearest_remaining\n    cent_term = 0.08 * (1.0 - progress) * mean_remaining\n    return -distance + rw * return_distance + rgw * regret + cl_term - cent_term",
  "source": "live_llm",
  "parent_id": 20,
  "reference_id": null,
  "action": "develop",
